Subject: [PATCH 31/40] Metal diamond engine: z wrap without a branch, the y
 width by a multiplication, whole SIMD groups (snapshot cg30c)

OPENEMS_DIAMOND_FASTIDX (default on): the z neighbour of the first and last z-vector comes from one load and a
select instead of a branch that half of each SIMD group takes, and the division of the cell index by the tile's width
in y, which changes with the half-step, is a multiplication. OPENEMS_DIAMOND_TGFLAG (default on): the pipeline is
told that a threadgroup is a whole number of SIMD groups, checked against the pipeline's execution width. Together
1-3 % on the GCPW line and the notch tutorial (loaded machine). diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical.

